1
00:00:01,799 --> 00:00:05,798
Chapter 15. Chowder.

2
00:00:05,799 --> 00:00:10,278
It was quite late in the evening when the little moss came snugly to anchor,

3
00:00:10,279 --> 00:00:15,078
and Quequake and I went ashore, so we could attend to no business that day, at

4
00:00:15,079 --> 00:00:19,558
least none but a supper and a bed. The landlord of the Spouter Inn had

5
00:00:19,559 --> 00:00:24,599
recommended us to his cousin, Hosea Hussy of the Tripots, whom he asserted

6
00:00:24,600 --> 00:00:29,238
to be the proprietor of one of the bestkept hotels in all Nantucket. And

7
00:00:29,239 --> 00:00:34,039
moreover, he had assured us that cousin Hosea, as he called him, was famous for

8
00:00:34,040 --> 00:00:38,679
his chowters. In short, he plainly hinted that we could not possibly do

9
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:41,718
better than tripot lock at the tripods.

10
00:00:41,719 --> 00:00:45,317
But the directions he had given us about keeping a yellow warehouse on our

11
00:00:45,318 --> 00:00:49,317
starboard hand till we opened a white church to the Larbird, and then keeping

12
00:00:49,318 --> 00:00:53,477
that on the Larbird hand till we made a corner three points to the starboard,

13
00:00:53,478 --> 00:00:57,798
and that done. then asked the first man we met where the place was. These

14
00:00:57,799 --> 00:01:02,199
crooked directions of his very much puzzled us at first, especially as at

15
00:01:02,200 --> 00:01:06,278
the outset Quiquake insisted that the yellow warehouse, our first point of

16
00:01:06,279 --> 00:01:11,397
