54
00:04:00,200 --> 00:04:05,317
But when that smoking chowder came in, the mystery was delightfully explained.

55
00:04:05,318 --> 00:04:11,238
"Oh, sweet friends, hearken to me. It was made of small juicy clams scarcely

56
00:04:11,239 --> 00:04:15,958
bigger than hazelnuts, mixed with pounded ship biscuit and salted pork cut

57
00:04:15,959 --> 00:04:19,798
up into little flakes, the whole enriched with butter and plentifully

58
00:04:19,799 --> 00:04:24,119
seasoned with pepper and salt. Our appetites being sharpened by the frosty

59
00:04:24,120 --> 00:04:28,519
voyage, and in particular Quequake, seeing his favorite fishing food before

60
00:04:28,520 --> 00:04:33,238
him, and the chowder being surpassingly excellent, we dispatched it with great

61
00:04:33,239 --> 00:04:38,199
expedition. When leaning back a moment, and bethinking me of Mrs. Tussy's clam

62
00:04:38,200 --> 00:04:42,759
and cod announcement. I thought I would try a little experiment. Stepping to the

63
00:04:42,760 --> 00:04:48,519
kitchen door, I uttered the word cod with great emphasis and resumed my seat.

64
00:04:48,520 --> 00:04:53,238
In a few moments the savory steam came forth again, but with a different

65
00:04:53,239 --> 00:04:59,158
flavor, and in good time a fine cod chowder was placed before us. We resumed

66
00:04:59,159 --> 00:05:03,878
business, and while pllying our spoons in the bowl, thinks I to myself, I

67
00:05:03,879 --> 00:05:08,519
wonder now if this here has any effect on the head. What's that stoaltifying

68
00:05:08,520 --> 00:05:13,317
saying about chowder-headed people? But look, Quiquake, ain't that a live eel in

69
00:05:13,318 --> 00:05:16,679
